# Line endings belong to the repository, not to each clone's core.autocrlf. Without this, a checkout on Windows
# converts the tree to CRLF and every `git add` warns that it is about to, on every file.

# Text is stored LF and checked out LF. Git works out for itself what is text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the two kinds of file Visual Studio writes and rewrites itself, which it writes CRLF. Storing them LF and
# checking them out CRLF keeps them readable in a diff without VS reformatting them back on every save.
*.sln  text eol=crlf
*.resx text eol=crlf
